{"id":"ch-ajo","title":"Update WorkflowEngine to handle CREATE vs UPDATE events","description":"Update WorkflowEngine.startEventProcessing() to distinguish between CREATE events (that start workflows) and UPDATE events (that modify existing workflows).

CURRENT BEHAVIOR:
All events trigger workflow creation + execution

NEW BEHAVIOR:
1. **CREATE events**: Create WorkflowState + start execution (existing behavior)
2. **UPDATE events**: Find/update existing workflow, or create new

PSEUDOCODE:
```typescript
const eventResult = yield* registry.handleEvent(event);

if (eventResult._tag === "CreateWorkflow") {
  // Create new workflow
  yield* workflowMutation.create({
    id: eventResult.workflowId,
    workflowType: eventResult.workflowType,
    progressData: eventResult.progress
  });

  // Execute immediately
  yield* execute(eventResult.workflowId);
}

if (eventResult._tag === "UpdateWorkflow") {
  if (eventResult.isNew) {
    // Create new workflow (first occurrence)
    yield* workflowMutation.create({
      id: eventResult.workflowId,
      workflowType: eventResult.workflowType,
      progressData: eventResult.progress
    });
  } else {
    // Update existing workflow
    yield* workflowMutation.updateProgress({
      id: eventResult.workflowId,
      progressData: eventResult.progress
    });
  }

  // Don't execute - running workflow picks up changes at checkpoint
}
```

REGISTRY CHANGES NEEDED:
handleEvent needs to return tagged union:
```typescript
type HandleEventResult = 
  | { _tag: "CreateWorkflow"; workflowId: WorkflowId; workflowType: string; progress: unknown }
  | { _tag: "UpdateWorkflow"; workflowId: WorkflowId; workflowType: string; progress: unknown; isNew: boolean }
  | { _tag: "Ignored" }
```

